	(text "Simulated design only: nothing built in hardware.\nSix-step (trapezoidal) drive: in each 60 deg sector one high side switches at 20 kHz with its low side as\nsynchronous rectifier, one low side is on, one leg floats. Dead time (500 ns) is inserted by the firmware\n(compare pair per leg, src/bldc/bldc.c); the IR2101 has no internal interlock, so the MCU timing is the\nonly protection against shoot-through (sim/ngspice/leg_deadtime.cir: shoot-through below about 250 ns).\nGate pull-downs (R13/R14...) hold the bridge off while the MCU is in reset; R71-R76 hold the driver inputs low.\nRS1 2.5 mOhm + U4 INA181A1 (gain 20): ISENSE = 1.65 V + 50 mV/A, sampled at the PWM counter peak.\nVBUS_SNS = VBUS / 11. Hall sensors: open collector, 12 V supply, 4.7k pull-ups to 3.3 V, 1k / 1 nF filter.\nJ5 goes to the MCU: PWM_xH / PWM_xL from a centre-aligned timer, HALL_A-C to GPIO, ISENSE / VBUS_SNS to ADC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 292.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1b6d0ec2-f70a-5719-ae43-f8730a935ea1")
	)
